0
00:00:08,046 --> 00:00:10,047
PREVIOUSLY ON
"AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL,"

1
00:00:10,047 --> 00:00:12,050
I JOINED THE FINAL FIVE
FOR DINNER,

2
00:00:12,050 --> 00:00:14,019
AND THINGS GOT EMOTIONAL.

3
00:00:14,019 --> 00:00:16,688
I FEEL SO LUCKY BECAUSE
WE ACTUALLY ARE FRIENDS.

4
00:00:16,688 --> 00:00:19,491
THE GIRLS MET SOUTH AFRICA'S
FASHION ELITE...

5
00:00:19,491 --> 00:00:20,992
HI, I'M KEENYAH.

6
00:00:20,992 --> 00:00:24,496
AND GOT A TASTE OF
KEENYAH'S COMPETITIVE SIDE.

7
00:00:24,496 --> 00:00:27,399
AND KEENYAH LOVED
THE LOCAL CUISINE.

8
00:00:27,399 --> 00:00:28,900
OH, GOT YOU!

9
00:00:28,900 --> 00:00:30,135
YEAH.

10
00:00:30,135 --> 00:00:32,137
IN THE END,
CHRISTINA COULDN'T THAW

11
00:00:32,137 --> 00:00:33,138
HER COLD PERSONA...

12
00:00:33,138 --> 00:00:35,140
I'M NOT FEELING ANYTHING
FROM YOU.

13
00:00:35,140 --> 00:00:36,942
AND SHE WAS SENT HOME.

14
00:00:36,942 --> 00:00:40,412
FOUR GIRLS REMAIN-- NAIMA,
KEENYAH, KAHLEN AND BRITTANY.

15
00:00:40,412 --> 00:00:43,615
WHO WILL BE ELIMINATED TONIGHT?

16
00:00:43,615 --> 00:00:47,853
♪♪♪

17
00:01:26,258 --> 00:01:29,161
♪♪♪

18
00:01:33,465 --> 00:01:36,168
OKAY, THANKS, BRITT.

19
00:01:36,168 --> 00:01:37,669
YOU'RE WELCOME.

20
00:01:37,669 --> 00:01:40,071
HEY, YOU'RE WELCOME.

21
00:01:40,071 --> 00:01:43,141
THERE ARE FOUR OF US NOW,
AND I THINK KEENYAH AND BRITTANY

22
00:01:43,141 --> 00:01:46,311
HAVE MADE A FRIENDSHIP WHERE
THEY CAN SUPPORT EACH OTHER.

23
00:01:46,311 --> 00:01:49,080
AND KAHLEN HAS BEEN
MY BEST FRIEND

24
00:01:49,080 --> 00:01:50,081
IN THIS COMPETITION.

25
00:01:50,081 --> 00:01:51,983
SHE HAS BEEN
MY EMOTIONAL SUPPORT.

26
00:01:56,855 --> 00:01:59,691
YOU ALL ARE SO USED TO
BEING JUDGED BY US, THIS WEEK

27
00:01:59,691 --> 00:02:02,561
YOU'RE GOING TO JUDGE
EACH OTHER.

28
00:02:02,561 --> 00:02:04,729
HAVING MY COMPETITORS
JUDGE ME,

29
00:02:04,729 --> 00:02:08,800
IT WAS VERY HARD, BUT I THINK
OVERALL, IT'S IMPORTANT

30
00:02:08,800 --> 00:02:10,502
IN A COMPETITION.

31
00:02:10,502 --> 00:02:11,837
THE PERSON WHO I THINK
MAY HAVE

32
00:02:11,837 --> 00:02:14,172
THE LEAST POTENTIAL IN THIS,
I WOULD PROBABLY

33
00:02:14,172 --> 00:02:15,240
HAVE TO SAY NAIMA.

34
00:02:15,240 --> 00:02:17,776
I THINK THERE'S A SHELL
AROUND HER SOMETIMES.

35
00:02:17,776 --> 00:02:20,445
NAIMA'S PERSONALITY IS NOT
VERY OUTGOING.

36
00:02:20,445 --> 00:02:22,314
PEOPLE AREN'T GONNA RELATE
TO HER AS MUCH

37
00:02:22,314 --> 00:02:25,884
AS THEY WOULD RELATE TO LIKE
BRITTANY OR, YOU KNOW, TO ME.

38
00:02:25,884 --> 00:02:28,353
THE WHOLE POINT
OF THAT CHALLENGE WAS TO SEE

39
00:02:28,353 --> 00:02:29,721
HOW MUCH WE'VE LEARNED.

40
00:02:29,721 --> 00:02:32,557
SO IF THAT MEANS I HAVE TO
PINPOINT EVERY LITTLE THING

41
00:02:32,557 --> 00:02:35,260
THAT MAYBE THEY WOULD SAY,
THEN I'M GONNA DO THAT.

42
00:02:35,260 --> 00:02:38,096
THE THING THAT ANNOYS ME
WITH KEENYAH IS SHE DOESN'T PUT

43
00:02:38,096 --> 00:02:39,297
OTHER PEOPLE AHEAD OF HER.

44
00:02:39,297 --> 00:02:41,299
IT'S ALWAYS KEENYAH,
KEENYAH, KEENYAH.

45
00:02:41,299 --> 00:02:44,269
SO I REALLY DIDN'T CARE
WHO WAS MY FRIEND AT THAT TIME.

46
00:02:44,269 --> 00:02:45,537
I WAS REALLY SHOWING THEM
THAT I--

47
00:02:45,537 --> 00:02:46,204
Brittany: I CAN'T BELIEVE
THE WAY YOU SAID--

48
00:02:46,204 --> 00:02:48,206
CAN I FINISH TALKING,
BRITTANY, PLEASE?

49
00:02:48,206 --> 00:02:49,908
I JUST WANT TO FINISH
THIS SENTENCE.

50
00:02:49,908 --> 00:02:51,176
OKAY, DON'T EVER GET RUDE
WITH ME LIKE THAT AGAIN

51
00:02:51,176 --> 00:02:52,978
'CAUSE YOU CUT PEOPLE OFF
ALL OF THE TIME.

52
00:02:52,978 --> 00:02:54,145
I KNOW, I AM LEARNING THAT.

53
00:02:54,145 --> 00:02:55,847
BUT YOU--
I'VE ASKED YOU ALREADY.

54
00:02:55,847 --> 00:02:58,149
I AM NOT FINISHED TALKING,
BUT YOU STILL GO.

55
00:02:58,149 --> 00:03:01,620
WE'VE BEEN TOGETHER SO LONG,
LITTLE THINGS THAT MAYBE

56
00:03:01,620 --> 00:03:03,855
WOULDN'T HAVE BOTHERED US
IN THE VERY BEGINNING

57
00:03:03,855 --> 00:03:06,691
WHEN WE WERE JUST STARTING OFF
ARE JUST IRRITATING NOW.

58
00:03:06,691 --> 00:03:08,426
YOU DIDN'T LET ME FINISH.

59
00:03:08,426 --> 00:03:10,228
I WANT TO FINISH.

60
00:03:16,401 --> 00:03:17,736
♪♪♪
WE GOT TYRA MAIL.

61
00:03:17,736 --> 00:03:18,837
"IN THIS
MODELING COMPETITION,

62
00:03:18,837 --> 00:03:19,838
EVERY STEP COUNTS.

63
00:03:19,838 --> 00:03:22,107
BE READY AT 9:45 A.M."

64
00:03:22,107 --> 00:03:24,442
"EVERY STEP COUNTS"?

65
00:03:24,442 --> 00:03:26,745
HOW OBVIOUS IS THAT?

66
00:03:26,745 --> 00:03:29,114
IT'S OBVIOUS? WHAT IS IT?

67
00:03:29,114 --> 00:03:32,350
IS THAT THAT CHOCOLATE THING?

68
00:03:32,350 --> 00:03:32,918
WHAT?

69
00:03:32,918 --> 00:03:35,553
EATING IS LIKE-- I DON'T KNOW,
IT MAKES ME FEEL BETTER.

70
00:03:35,553 --> 00:03:38,390
I DON'T KNOW WHAT KIND
OF SYNDROME I HAVE.

71
00:03:38,390 --> 00:03:40,392
IS THAT THAT CHOCOLATE--
WHAT IS THAT IN YOUR HAND?

72
00:03:40,392 --> 00:03:41,026
YEAH,
IT'S A CHOCOLATE MUFFIN.

73
00:03:41,026 --> 00:03:42,560
BUT WHAT ARE YOU TALKING ABOUT
WITH THE TYRA MAIL?

74
00:03:42,560 --> 00:03:43,662
YOU REALLY THINK IT'S
THAT OBVIOUS?

75
00:03:43,662 --> 00:03:45,397
YOU THINK IT'S RUNWAY AGAIN?

76
00:03:45,397 --> 00:03:46,598
I HOPE IT IS.

77
00:03:46,598 --> 00:03:50,468
NOW, I REAL, LIKE-- CAN I HAVE
A LITTLE PIECE OF IT?

78
00:03:50,468 --> 00:03:51,870
UH-HUH.

79
00:03:51,870 --> 00:03:53,338
WOULD YOU FINISH,
YOUR GOSH DARN THOUGHT?

80
00:03:53,338 --> 00:03:55,974
I FEEL LIKE IT'S GONNA BE
A RUNWAY SHOW.

81
00:03:55,974 --> 00:03:58,009
I DON'T THINK KEENYAH
IS WATCHING WHAT SHE EATS.

82
00:03:58,009 --> 00:03:59,611
THAT'S WHAT THE JUDGES
KEEP TELLING HER,

83
00:03:59,611 --> 00:04:01,713
IT'S WHAT THEY KEEP
COMPLAINING ABOUT.

84
00:04:01,713 --> 00:04:06,484
AND I REALLY DON'T SEE
THAT MUCH PROGRESS... AT ALL.

85
00:04:06,484 --> 00:04:09,387
♪♪♪

86
00:04:14,259 --> 00:04:18,463
CAN I WEAR THIS, UM,
WHAT'S YOUR NAME, BRITTANY?

87
00:04:18,463 --> 00:04:19,464
WHAT'S YOUR NAME?

88
00:04:19,464 --> 00:04:21,399
YOU CAN BORROW WHATEVER
YOU WANT OF MINE.

89
00:04:21,399 --> 00:04:22,466
BECAUSE I'M SPECIAL.

90
00:04:22,466 --> 00:04:24,468
SAY "BECAUSE YOU'RE SPECIAL"
AT THE END OF IT.

91
00:04:24,468 --> 00:04:26,638
SAY IT AGAIN.

92
00:04:26,638 --> 00:04:29,908
'CAUSE YOU'RE SPECIAL.

93
00:04:29,908 --> 00:04:32,177
COOL. COOL, COOL, COOL.

94
00:04:32,177 --> 00:04:37,649
♪♪♪
RIGHT HERE, GUYS.

95
00:04:37,649 --> 00:04:38,650
HI, YOU GUYS.

96
00:04:38,650 --> 00:04:39,150
HELLO.

97
00:04:39,150 --> 00:04:40,151
HOW ARE YOU DOING?

98
00:04:40,151 --> 00:04:41,152
GOOD. HOW ARE YOU?

99
00:04:41,152 --> 00:04:42,520
I'M FINE. I AM BEBE.

100
00:04:42,520 --> 00:04:44,222
HE IS MANDELA MOKOENA.

101
00:04:44,222 --> 00:04:45,223
PLEASURE TO MEET YOU.

102
00:04:45,223 --> 00:04:47,225
TOGETHER,
WE'RE THE COFOUNDERS

103
00:04:47,225 --> 00:04:49,995
OF G'MBO URBAN ETHNIC CLOTHING.

104
00:04:49,995 --> 00:04:52,030
IT'S A PROUDLY
SOUTH AFRICAN BRAND,

105
00:04:52,030 --> 00:04:55,367
SOUTH AFRICA COMES FROM
A PRETTY ROUGH BACKGROUND.

106
00:04:55,367 --> 00:04:59,204
WE JUST GOT DEMOCRACY
JUST ABOUT TEN YEARS AGO.

107
00:04:59,204 --> 00:05:03,008
SO WE WANTED TO WEAR SOMETHING
THAT WOULD REFLECT WHO WE ARE

108
00:05:03,008 --> 00:05:05,944
AND WHERE WE COME FROM
AND WHERE WE WANT TO GO.

109
00:05:05,944 --> 00:05:10,348
SO WE'RE GOING TO SHOW YOU
WHAT IT IS LIKE IN THE TOWNSHIPS

110
00:05:10,348 --> 00:05:13,218
AND WHERE WE DERIVE
SOME OF OUR INSPIRATION.

111
00:05:16,221 --> 00:05:19,124
THESE ARE
THE INFORMAL SETTLEMENTS,

112
00:05:19,124 --> 00:05:20,325
SHACKS.

113
00:05:20,325 --> 00:05:22,627
A TOWNSHIP IS BASICALLY
WHAT WE CALL THE GHETTO

114
00:05:22,627 --> 00:05:23,862
BACK IN AMERICA.

115
00:05:23,862 --> 00:05:25,864
IT'S LIKE LITTLE METAL,
LIKE SHACKS LIKE

116
00:05:25,864 --> 00:05:28,433
WITH PLASTIC BAGS FOR ROOFS.

117
00:05:31,669 --> 00:05:33,338
THEY'RE NOT
LIKE THIS, THOUGH.

118
00:05:33,338 --> 00:05:35,173
THIS IS, TO ME, VERY EXTREME.

119
00:05:35,173 --> 00:05:36,241
YEAH.

120
00:05:36,241 --> 00:05:39,477
THIS IS NOT DECENT LIVING
BY ANY MEANS AND STANDARDS.

121
00:05:39,477 --> 00:05:40,445
NOT WHAT?

122
00:05:40,445 --> 00:05:42,747
DECENT LIVING.

123
00:05:42,747 --> 00:05:45,817
THIS IS NOT-- THIS IS NOT LIFE.

124
00:05:45,817 --> 00:05:48,653
YOU SEE IT ON TV,
BUT WHEN YOU'RE ACTUALLY IN IT,

125
00:05:48,653 --> 00:05:52,757
AND YOU SEE IT, IT'S LIKE,
WOW, THIS REALLY DOES EXIST.

126
00:05:55,493 --> 00:05:57,495
WE SHOW UP
AT THE COMMUNITY CENTER

127
00:05:57,495 --> 00:05:59,898
IN THE TOWNSHIP.

128
00:06:00,031 --> 00:06:05,270
(speaking indistinctly)
THIS IS JACKIE FROM JAZZ ART.

129
00:06:05,270 --> 00:06:07,405
HI, I'M JACKIE MANYAPELO.

130
00:06:07,405 --> 00:06:08,540
HI.

131
00:06:08,540 --> 00:06:10,442
WE'RE THE JAZZ ART
DANCE THEATER.

132
00:06:10,442 --> 00:06:13,144
TODAY YOU'LL BE LEARNING
ABOUT RHYTHM AND DANCE.

133
00:06:13,144 --> 00:06:18,083
I GOTTA SAY, I DO NOT KNOW
HOW THIS IS GONNA GO.

134
00:06:18,083 --> 00:06:20,085
YOU'LL BE PAIRED UP
WITH AN INSTRUCTOR,

135
00:06:20,085 --> 00:06:22,487
SO LET'S GET STARTED.

136
00:06:22,487 --> 00:06:23,855
I HATE DANCING.

137
00:06:23,855 --> 00:06:26,791
I DON'T EVEN KNOW
WHAT TRIBAL DANCING IS.

138
00:06:26,791 --> 00:06:28,726
YOU DON'T WANT ME
BECAUSE I CAN'T DANCE.

139
00:06:28,726 --> 00:06:29,794
I KNOW.

140
00:06:29,794 --> 00:06:32,297
THIS IS GONNA BE EMBARRASSING.

141
00:06:32,297 --> 00:06:34,566
OKAY.

142
00:06:34,566 --> 00:06:39,204
(gives dance commands)
I'VE ALWAYS THOUGHT

143
00:06:39,204 --> 00:06:42,540
THAT THERE WAS A CONNECTION
BETWEEN DANCE AND MODELING.

144
00:06:42,540 --> 00:06:46,911
IT HELPS YOU REALIZE YOUR BODY
AS A WHOLE PIECE OF MOVEMENT.

145
00:06:46,911 --> 00:06:48,947
UP, CATCH.

146
00:06:48,947 --> 00:06:50,949
I'M IN AFRICA
WHERE MY PEOPLE ARE FROM,

147
00:06:50,949 --> 00:06:52,951
SO I SHOULD FEEL
EVEN MORE EMPOWERED,

148
00:06:52,951 --> 00:06:54,953
LIKE I AM WHERE I'M FROM NOW.

149
00:06:54,953 --> 00:06:56,721
AND SO I REALLY SHOULD BRING IT.

150
00:06:56,721 --> 00:06:59,124
OH!

151
00:06:59,124 --> 00:07:01,025
MY JEANS ARE TOO TIGHT.

152
00:07:03,027 --> 00:07:04,896
I DON'T DANCE.

153
00:07:04,896 --> 00:07:07,465
NOT AT ALL.

154
00:07:07,465 --> 00:07:09,767
ESPECIALLY NOT
AFRICAN TRIBAL DANCE.

155
00:07:09,767 --> 00:07:11,836
I CAN'T GET INTO THE MOTIONS YET
BECAUSE I DON'T KNOW LIKE

156
00:07:11,836 --> 00:07:13,471
WHAT I'M DOING.

157
00:07:13,471 --> 00:07:18,109
KICK.

158
00:07:18,109 --> 00:07:21,312
I AM JUST WIGGLING AROUND
UP THERE.

159
00:07:21,312 --> 00:07:23,948
WHEN THINGS GET TOO HARD
IN MY LIFE, YOU KNOW, I GIVE UP

160
00:07:23,948 --> 00:07:27,018
BECAUSE I DON'T EVER
WANT TO FAIL.

161
00:07:27,018 --> 00:07:29,521
KAHLEN LET IT BUILD
AND BUILD AND BUILD.

162
00:07:29,521 --> 00:07:33,124
IT MADE HER FEEL EVEN WORSE
ABOUT YOURSELF.

163
00:07:33,124 --> 00:07:34,492
I NEED A WATER.

164
00:07:34,492 --> 00:07:36,494
IS THIS YOUR FIRST TIME
IN AFRICA FOR ALL OF YOU?

165
00:07:36,494 --> 00:07:37,495
MM-HMM, ALL OF US.

166
00:07:37,495 --> 00:07:38,563
IT'S GOOD TO COME HERE.

167
00:07:38,563 --> 00:07:40,565
NOT THAT IT'S MORE IMPORTANT
TO ME THEM

168
00:07:40,565 --> 00:07:41,566
BECAUSE THEY'RE NOT BLACK.

169
00:07:41,566 --> 00:07:42,700
I'M BLACK.

170
00:07:42,700 --> 00:07:45,403
KEENYAH'S JUST LIKE, "I'M BLACK,
I'M BLACK,

171
00:07:45,403 --> 00:07:46,938
AND THIS MEANS A LOT TO ME."

172
00:07:46,938 --> 00:07:49,274
AND I'M JUST LIKE,
"WELL, KEENYAH,

173
00:07:49,274 --> 00:07:51,309
DON'T YOU SEE ME SITTING HERE?"

174
00:07:51,309 --> 00:07:53,344
OF COURSE, I DON'T HAVE
DARK BROWN SKIN,

175
00:07:53,344 --> 00:07:57,448
BUT MY FATHER IS BLACK,
AND MEXICAN INDIAN,

176
00:07:57,448 --> 00:08:00,151
AND MY MOM IS BLACK AND IRISH.

177
00:08:00,151 --> 00:08:02,153
COMING FROM AMERICA,
BEING BLACK, LIKE

178
00:08:02,153 --> 00:08:04,522
I WAS LIKE, "BEFORE I DIE
I HAVE TO GO TO AFRICA."

179
00:08:04,522 --> 00:08:06,157
IT FEELS GOOD TO BE HERE.

180
00:08:06,157 --> 00:08:07,225
THANK YOU.

181
00:08:07,225 --> 00:08:08,393
WELCOME HOME.

182
00:08:08,393 --> 00:08:10,228
SOME OF THEM ARE SAYING
TO ME LIKE, "WELCOME HOME,

183
00:08:10,228 --> 00:08:12,230
WELCOME HOME," AND THEY'RE NOT
SAYING IT TO THE OTHER GIRLS.

184
00:08:12,230 --> 00:08:13,898
I FEEL VERY GOOD
THAT THEY SAY THAT TO ME.

185
00:08:14,899 --> 00:08:16,034
OKAY.

186
00:08:16,034 --> 00:08:18,036
SO YOU'VE LEARNED THE DANCE.

187
00:08:18,036 --> 00:08:19,604
YOU KNOW IT.

188
00:08:19,604 --> 00:08:21,606
AND NOW YOU'RE GONNA BE
PERFORMING IT

189
00:08:21,606 --> 00:08:24,209
IN FRONT OF AN AUDIENCE.

190
00:08:24,209 --> 00:08:26,678
THERE ARE TIMES WHERE,
YOU KNOW, ULTIMATE

191
00:08:26,678 --> 00:08:29,180
AND TOTAL HUMILIATION
IS JUST NOT SOMETHING

192
00:08:29,180 --> 00:08:30,748
I WANT TO THROW MYSELF INTO.

193
00:08:30,748 --> 00:08:32,850
I DO A PRETTY GOOD JOB OF THAT
BY MYSELF.

194
00:08:32,850 --> 00:08:37,822
IT IS A CHALLENGE,
AND YOU WILL BE JUDGED.

195
00:08:37,822 --> 00:08:40,758
THIS IS ALFRED HINKLE,
ARTISTIC DIRECTOR OF JAZZ ART.

196
00:08:40,758 --> 00:08:44,329
WE'VE ALSO GOT A SPECIAL GUEST.

197
00:08:44,329 --> 00:08:47,231
(laughter)

198
00:08:49,500 --> 00:08:51,135
WHAT'S UP, GIRLS?

199
00:08:51,135 --> 00:08:52,303
HEY.

200
00:08:52,303 --> 00:08:53,538
WHAT'S GOING ON?

201
00:08:53,538 --> 00:08:55,540
IT'S VERY NICE
TO SEE MISS J.,

202
00:08:55,540 --> 00:08:57,942
BUT I DON'T WANT TO DANCE
IN FRONT OF HIM.

203
00:08:57,942 --> 00:08:59,477
YOU GONNA SHOW ME
WHAT YOU GOT?

204
00:08:59,477 --> 00:09:00,511
YES.

205
00:09:00,511 --> 00:09:01,713
OKAY. GOOD.

206
00:09:01,713 --> 00:09:03,615
GO BACK
INTO THE DRESSING ROOM,

207
00:09:03,615 --> 00:09:04,716
GET YOUR COSTUME ON.
IT'S SHOW TIME.

208
00:09:13,324 --> 00:09:15,326
I'M GONNA LOOK
SO GOOFY OUT THERE.

209
00:09:15,326 --> 00:09:17,095
OH, GOD.

210
00:09:22,500 --> 00:09:24,836
DANCING'S ONE THING
I CAN'T DO,

211
00:09:24,836 --> 00:09:26,838
AND I NEVER WANT TO BE
ON THE STAGE DANCING.

212
00:09:26,838 --> 00:09:28,439
I HATE THIS CHALLENGE!

213
00:09:28,439 --> 00:09:32,543
IT'S-- IT'S FRUSTRATING,
REALLY FRUSTRATING FOR ME.

214
00:09:37,015 --> 00:09:41,552
(singing in African language)

215
00:09:44,054 --> 00:09:46,056
TODAY'S CHALLENGE,
WE'RE GONNA BE JUDGED

216
00:09:46,056 --> 00:09:48,058
ON HOW WELL WE CAN MOVE
AND HOW WELL WE'VE LEARNED

217
00:09:48,058 --> 00:09:49,860
THE ACTUAL CHOREOGRAPHY.

218
00:09:49,860 --> 00:09:52,930
YOU'VE LEARNED THE DANCE,
AND NOW YOU'RE GONNA BE

219
00:09:52,930 --> 00:09:54,999
PERFORMING IT
IN FRONT OF AN AUDIENCE.

220
00:09:54,999 --> 00:09:56,934
I'M JUST LIKE,
"OKAY, LET ME JUST

221
00:09:56,934 --> 00:09:58,802
ROLL WITH THE PUNCHES
AND SEE IF I CAN DO THIS."

222
00:10:02,640 --> 00:10:05,542
(making rattling noise)

223
00:10:15,286 --> 00:10:18,188
♪♪♪

224
00:10:21,692 --> 00:10:25,429
(cheering and screaming)

225
00:10:30,868 --> 00:10:32,870
THE AUDIENCE
DIDN'T LIKE MY DANCE.

226
00:10:32,870 --> 00:10:36,006
I DON'T BLAME THEM.

227
00:10:41,912 --> 00:10:43,847
GOT UP, YOU KNOW,
IN FRONT ON THAT STAGE,

228
00:10:43,847 --> 00:10:44,949
IN FRONT OF THE AUDIENCE.

229
00:10:44,949 --> 00:10:46,450
OF COURSE, I WAS VERY NERVOUS.

230
00:10:46,450 --> 00:10:47,484
BUT I ACTED.

231
00:10:47,484 --> 00:10:49,486
I ACTED THE ENTIRE TIME
I WAS UP THERE

232
00:10:49,486 --> 00:10:50,721
BECAUSE I WAS UNCOMFORTABLE.

233
00:10:50,721 --> 00:10:53,857
KAHLEN NEVER THINKS
THAT SHE DID GOOD

234
00:10:53,857 --> 00:10:56,093
OR SHE'S DOING GOOD
OR DOES GOOD,

235
00:10:56,093 --> 00:10:59,763
AND SHE ALWAYS DOES.

236
00:11:02,533 --> 00:11:06,303
I FEEL VERY HONORED
AND VERY BLESSED TO ACTUALLY

237
00:11:06,303 --> 00:11:08,372
LEARN SOME AFRICAN DANCE.

238
00:11:08,372 --> 00:11:10,874
ME BEING THE ONLY BLACK GIRL,
NOT THAT I APPRECIATE IT

239
00:11:10,874 --> 00:11:13,243
MORE THAN EVERYBODY ELSE
BECAUSE THEY'RE NOT BLACK,

240
00:11:13,243 --> 00:11:17,982
BUT THIS IS VERY
IMPORTANT TO ME.

241
00:11:17,982 --> 00:11:21,151
BEING A QUIET PERSON HAS
ALWAYS BEEN PART OF WHO I AM.

242
00:11:21,151 --> 00:11:25,022
FOR ME, BECAUSE I'VE BEEN
LIKE TRAINING IN BALLET FOR

243
00:11:25,022 --> 00:11:29,426
SO LONG, DANCING HAS GIVEN ME
AN OUTLET TO EXPRESS MYSELF

244
00:11:29,426 --> 00:11:32,830
WITHOUT SPEAKING.

245
00:11:32,830 --> 00:11:37,668
(applause)

246
00:11:50,414 --> 00:11:53,417
TO PERFORM IN FRONT
OF AFRICAN PEOPLE WHO LIVE HERE

247
00:11:53,417 --> 00:11:56,553
IN THE TOWNSHIP,
IT WAS LIKE REALLY COOL.

248
00:11:56,553 --> 00:11:58,789
LIKE I FEEL VERY, VERY GOOD
ABOUT MYSELF.

249
00:11:58,789 --> 00:12:02,626
I WOULD LIKE TO ASK
THE AUDIENCE--

250
00:12:02,626 --> 00:12:06,397
WHO DO YOU THINK WAS THE BEST?

251
00:12:06,397 --> 00:12:07,564
KEENYAH?

252
00:12:07,564 --> 00:12:12,202
(cheers and applause)
THERE YOU GO.

253
00:12:12,202 --> 00:12:13,771
OKAY.

254
00:12:13,771 --> 00:12:15,072
BRITTANY.

255
00:12:15,072 --> 00:12:18,375
(applause)
KAHLEN.

256
00:12:18,375 --> 00:12:21,478
(applause)
NAIMA.

257
00:12:21,478 --> 00:12:23,847
(loud cheers and applause)
OUR WINNER TODAY

258
00:12:23,847 --> 00:12:24,848
IS MISS NAIMA.

259
00:12:24,848 --> 00:12:29,353
(applause)

260
00:12:29,353 --> 00:12:31,622
NAIMA REALLY DESERVED IT.

261
00:12:31,622 --> 00:12:34,158
SHE DID A GREAT JOB,
SO I CAN'T BE BITTER,

262
00:12:34,158 --> 00:12:35,726
THOUGH I WOULD LOVE TO BE.

263
00:12:35,726 --> 00:12:38,962
FOR THE WINNER
OF THIS COMPETITION,

264
00:12:38,962 --> 00:12:44,768
YOU GET AN EXTRA 30 FRAMES
ON YOUR NEXT PHOTO SHOOT.

265
00:12:44,768 --> 00:12:49,573
YOU ALSO GET TO CHOOSE ONE GIRL
THAT WILL GET AN EXTRA 20 FRAMES

266
00:12:49,573 --> 00:12:51,275
ON HER NEXT PHOTO SHOOT.

267
00:12:51,275 --> 00:12:53,777
SO WHO WILL BE THE LUCKY GIRL?

268
00:12:53,777 --> 00:12:55,779
KEENYAH.

269
00:12:55,779 --> 00:12:57,781
NAIMA PICKS KEENYAH TO SHARE
THE PRIZE WITH,

270
00:12:57,781 --> 00:12:58,982
AND I'M NOT REALLY SURE WHY.

271
00:12:58,982 --> 00:13:00,784
I HAVE
A VERY STRONG FRIENDSHIP

272
00:13:00,784 --> 00:13:02,786
WITH KAHLEN,
BUT I HAVE TO THINK

273
00:13:02,786 --> 00:13:04,121
AS A COMPETITOR.

274
00:13:04,121 --> 00:13:06,457
HER PICTURES ARE ALREADY GREAT,
AND IF SHE GETS MORE FRAMES,

275
00:13:06,457 --> 00:13:09,493
IT'S GONNA GIVE ME LESS LIKELY
OF A CHANCE OF SURPASSING HER

276
00:13:09,493 --> 00:13:10,828
IN THE PANEL.

277
00:13:10,828 --> 00:13:15,399
NOW, KEENYAH, YOU GET
TO CHOOSE THE GIRL WHO GETS

278
00:13:15,399 --> 00:13:19,136
AN EXTRA TEN FRAMES
ON HER NEXT PHOTO SHOOT.

279
00:13:19,136 --> 00:13:20,771
BRITTANY.

280
00:13:20,771 --> 00:13:23,173
MISS BRITTANY,
YOU GET TO TELL

281
00:13:23,173 --> 00:13:27,544
MISS KAHLEN THAT SHE GETS NADA.

282
00:13:27,544 --> 00:13:29,580
SHE TAKES FABULOUS PICTURES,
SHE DOESN'T NEED

283
00:13:29,580 --> 00:13:31,181
ANY EXTRA FRAMES.

284
00:13:31,181 --> 00:13:33,851
SO, GIRLS, CONGRATULATIONS
AND GOOD LUCK.

285
00:13:33,851 --> 00:13:38,088
(cheers and applause)

286
00:13:40,958 --> 00:13:42,526
YOU DID BEAUTIFUL.

287
00:13:42,526 --> 00:13:43,527
THANK YOU.

288
00:13:43,527 --> 00:13:45,062
REALLY, WHY DID YOU PICK ME?

289
00:13:45,062 --> 00:13:47,064
'CAUSE YOU THINK I COULD
GET HELP IF I HAVE

290
00:13:47,064 --> 00:13:49,666
EXTRA FRAMES, RIGHT?

291
00:13:49,666 --> 00:13:52,970
AND SO I GET PICKED LAST,
AND I DON'T GET ANYTHING.

292
00:13:52,970 --> 00:13:55,339
IS THIS SOME KIND
OF SMALL ATTACK ON ME?

293
00:13:55,339 --> 00:13:56,473
YOU OKAY?

294
00:13:56,473 --> 00:13:58,275
YEAH, I'M FINE.

295
00:13:58,275 --> 00:13:59,443
WHAT'S GOING ON?

296
00:13:59,443 --> 00:14:01,278
WHAT IS THEIR MOTIVES
FOR DOING THIS?

297
00:14:01,278 --> 00:14:03,380
ARE THEY, YOU KNOW, JUST TRYING
TO GET RID OF ME?

298
00:14:03,380 --> 00:14:07,417
I JUST HOPE THAT THE REST OF
THIS COMPETITION GOES BY FAST,

299
00:14:07,417 --> 00:14:11,288
BECAUSE IT'S JUST
REALLY STARTING TO WEAR ON ME.

300
00:14:11,288 --> 00:14:14,525
♪♪♪

301
00:14:15,692 --> 00:14:17,561
TYRA MAIL.

302
00:14:17,561 --> 00:14:19,796
OKAY.

303
00:14:19,796 --> 00:14:22,432
"46664.

304
00:14:22,432 --> 00:14:25,135
"BE READY AT 11:00 A.M.

305
00:14:25,135 --> 00:14:26,270
TYRA."

306
00:14:26,270 --> 00:14:27,471
WHAT DOES THAT MEAN?

307
00:14:27,471 --> 00:14:30,307
I KNOW WHAT 666 IS,
BUT WHAT THE HELL IS THE 4s?

308
00:14:30,307 --> 00:14:33,810
46664-- I'M NOT
REALLY SURE WHAT IT MEANS.

309
00:14:33,810 --> 00:14:37,447
IT COULD BE A PIZZA
DELIVERY BOY'S PHONE NUMBER.

310
00:14:37,447 --> 00:14:42,753
♪♪♪
HI.

311
00:14:42,753 --> 00:14:43,954
WELCOME TO ROBBEN ISLAND.

312
00:14:43,954 --> 00:14:45,956
MY NAME IS MODISE,
AND ROBBEN ISLAND BASICALLY

313
00:14:45,956 --> 00:14:49,426
WAS MY HOME FOR FIVE YEARS
ROBBEN ISLAND WAS A PRISON.

314
00:14:49,426 --> 00:14:51,628
WE FIND OUT
THAT ROBBEN ISLAND WAS

315
00:14:51,628 --> 00:14:54,164
A POLITICAL PRISON
WHEN THERE WAS A LOT OF LIKE

316
00:14:54,164 --> 00:14:56,867
RACIAL SEGREGATION AND STUFF
GOING ON.

317
00:14:56,867 --> 00:14:58,702
A LOT OF PAIN,
LOT OF BEATING,

318
00:14:58,702 --> 00:14:59,970
LOT OF TORTURE.

319
00:14:59,970 --> 00:15:02,372
ROBBEN ISLAND WAS
NELSON MANDELA'S HOME

320
00:15:02,372 --> 00:15:05,075
FOR A PERIOD OF 18 YEARS.

321
00:15:05,075 --> 00:15:09,446
NELSON MANDELA WAS A MAN
WHO WAS A TRIBAL CHIEF.

322
00:15:09,446 --> 00:15:12,683
ULTIMATELY BECAME A LAWYER
TO BE IN THE STRUGGLE.

323
00:15:12,683 --> 00:15:15,319
HE WAS ARRESTED,
BROUGHT TO ROBBEN ISLAND.

324
00:15:15,319 --> 00:15:17,721
ON HIS RELEASE,
HE ROSE FROM THE ASHES

325
00:15:17,721 --> 00:15:19,756
OF ROBBEN ISLAND
TO BECOME THE FIRST

326
00:15:19,756 --> 00:15:23,961
ELECTED STATE PRESIDENT IN 1994
IN A NEW DEMOCRATIC

327
00:15:23,961 --> 00:15:25,996
SOUTH AFRICA.

328
00:15:25,996 --> 00:15:29,132
AS WE CAME HERE, YOU WILL BE
GIVEN A PRISON NUMBER,

329
00:15:29,132 --> 00:15:30,801
AND THAT WILL BE YOUR IDENTITY.

330
00:15:30,801 --> 00:15:34,705
MR. NELSON MANDELA-- THE NUMBER
IS KNOW AS 4-TRIPLE 6-4.

331
00:15:34,705 --> 00:15:38,642
THE NAME NELSON MANDELA
KEPT MY COUNTRY GOING.

332
00:15:38,642 --> 00:15:44,014
THE NAME NELSON MANDELA
KEPT MY PEOPLE HOPING.

333
00:15:44,014 --> 00:15:46,316
I DIDN'T KNOW
IF NELSON MANDELA, AT THE TIME,

334
00:15:46,316 --> 00:15:48,652
WAS ALIVE
OR NOT ALIVE AT THE MOMENT.

335
00:15:48,652 --> 00:15:49,853
OKAY, GUYS.

336
00:15:49,853 --> 00:15:52,489
KEENYAH ASKED ME, YOU KNOW,
"IS NELSON MANDELA

337
00:15:52,489 --> 00:15:54,191
EVEN STILL ALIVE?"

338
00:15:54,191 --> 00:15:56,026
AND I WAS LIKE, "YEAH."

339
00:15:56,026 --> 00:16:00,631
SO I DIDN'T THINK
THAT SHE KNEW MUCH ABOUT HIM.

340
00:16:00,631 --> 00:16:02,633
TODAY, I HOLD
THE MASTER KEY.

341
00:16:02,633 --> 00:16:06,236
I NEVER DREAMT OF HAVING
THIS KEY IN MY HAND.

342
00:16:06,236 --> 00:16:08,872
ONE OF YOU LADIES WILL HAVE
THE PLEASURE TO OPEN

343
00:16:08,872 --> 00:16:10,674
MR. MANDELA'S CELL.

344
00:16:10,674 --> 00:16:12,643
HE'S LIKE,
"WHICH ONE OF YOU GIRLS

345
00:16:12,643 --> 00:16:16,013
WOULD REALLY LIKE
TO OPEN THE CELL?"

346
00:16:16,013 --> 00:16:18,315
HE HANDS IT TO NAIMA,
YOU KNOW, AS NAIMA'S

347
00:16:18,315 --> 00:16:20,317
WALKING UP TO THE DOOR,
I LIKE I WISH I WAS

348
00:16:20,317 --> 00:16:21,518
OPENING IT.

349
00:16:21,518 --> 00:16:22,586
KEENYAH WANTED TO UNLOCK IT.

350
00:16:22,586 --> 00:16:24,521
YOU KNOW, LIKE SHE THINKS
JUST BECAUSE

351
00:16:24,521 --> 00:16:27,524
SHE'S THE BLACK ONE,
THAT SHE DESERVES TO OPEN IT.

352
00:16:27,524 --> 00:16:29,626
I DON'T REALLY THINK
OF NAIMA AS BLACK.

353
00:16:29,626 --> 00:16:32,696
I JUST DON'T SEE THAT IN HER.

354
00:16:32,696 --> 00:16:35,365
I'M NOT
THE TYPICAL BLACK GIRL,

355
00:16:35,365 --> 00:16:37,868
BUT IT MEANS A LOT FOR ME
BEING HERE.

356
00:16:37,868 --> 00:16:42,072
1964 TO 1982.

357
00:16:44,141 --> 00:16:48,945
JUST THE COURAGE
OF THAT ONE MAN KEPT US GOING.

358
00:16:52,616 --> 00:16:54,618
I DIDN'T EVEN THINK
THAT KEENYAH KNEW WHO HE WAS.

359
00:16:54,618 --> 00:16:56,620
SHE DOESN'T KNOW
IF HE'S ALIVE OR NOT,

360
00:16:56,620 --> 00:16:58,622
SO I DIDN'T UNDERSTAND
WHY SHE WAS GETTING

361
00:16:58,622 --> 00:16:59,956
SO EMOTIONAL.

362
00:16:59,956 --> 00:17:02,259
YOU PROBABLY
WEREN'T EMOTIONAL ABOUT IT,

363
00:17:02,259 --> 00:17:05,262
BUT I CRIED
WHEN I WENT IN NELSON--

364
00:17:05,262 --> 00:17:10,232
I WAS IN NELSON MANDELA'S CELL.

365
00:17:12,301 --> 00:17:14,704
DO YOU KNOW HOW BIG THAT IS?

366
00:17:14,704 --> 00:17:15,872
I GUESS.

367
00:17:15,872 --> 00:17:17,973
I MEAN, MAYBE IT REALLY DOES
MEAN A LOT TO KEENYAH.

368
00:17:17,973 --> 00:17:19,776
I JUST FEEL LIKE
IT'S SOMEWHAT FOR SHOW.

369
00:17:19,776 --> 00:17:21,812
I'VE HEARD HER SAY IT
SO MANY TIMES,

370
00:17:21,812 --> 00:17:23,747
"THIS JUST MEANS SO MUCH TO ME
'CAUSE I'M BLACK."

371
00:17:23,747 --> 00:17:26,482
AND IT'S JUST LIKE,
"OKAY, ALL RIGHT, GREAT."

372
00:17:28,218 --> 00:17:30,820
♪♪♪
TYRA MAIL.

373
00:17:30,820 --> 00:17:32,455
YES, TYRA MAIL.

374
00:17:32,455 --> 00:17:34,558
"ARE YOUR FEET AS HEAVY
AS YOUR LUGGAGE?

375
00:17:34,558 --> 00:17:36,660
FIND OUT TOMORROW AT 8:30."

376
00:17:36,660 --> 00:17:38,862
8:30 A.M.?

377
00:17:38,862 --> 00:17:41,898
♪♪♪

378
00:17:46,370 --> 00:17:47,404
HOW YOU GUYS DOIN'?

379
00:17:47,404 --> 00:17:48,605
GOOD.

380
00:17:48,605 --> 00:17:50,273
NO, WE'RE NOT
RIDING OSTRICHES TODAY, OKAY?

381
00:17:50,273 --> 00:17:51,475
LOOK AT 'EM.

382
00:17:51,475 --> 00:17:54,478
ON TODAY'S SHOOT WE'RE DOING
LIKE A 1940s PHOTOGRAPH

383
00:17:54,478 --> 00:17:57,981
FOR CARESS SENSATIONAL
SMOOTHING BODY WASH.

384
00:17:57,981 --> 00:18:00,484
AND THE SETTING IS HERE
AT THIS OSTRICH FARM.

385
00:18:00,484 --> 00:18:03,820
SO YOU GIRLS ARE KIND OF LIKE
THE ARISTOCRATIC WOMEN

386
00:18:03,820 --> 00:18:06,189
ON VACATION IN AFRICA.

387
00:18:06,189 --> 00:18:08,091
WE'RE GONNA HAVE
SOME AFRICAN DRUMMERS,

388
00:18:08,091 --> 00:18:10,494
AND YOU GUYS HAVE LEARNED
ALL ABOUT WHAT?

389
00:18:10,494 --> 00:18:11,762
MOVEMENT.

390
00:18:11,762 --> 00:18:14,598
SO TODAY'S REAL CHALLENGE IS
HOW WELL YOU CAN DANCE AND MOVE

391
00:18:14,598 --> 00:18:18,135
AND MAKE IT LOOK BELIEVABLE
AND BEAUTIFUL IN A PHOTOGRAPH.

392
00:18:18,135 --> 00:18:20,537
SO YOU GUYS HAD
A LITTLE COMPETITION THIS WEEK,

393
00:18:20,537 --> 00:18:22,172
AND WHO WON?

394
00:18:22,172 --> 00:18:23,273
NAIMA?

395
00:18:23,273 --> 00:18:25,108
OKAY, SO NORMALLY
WHEN WE DO A PHOTO SHOOT,

396
00:18:25,108 --> 00:18:27,744
WE GIVE EACH OF YOU GIRLS
70 FRAMES.

397
00:18:27,744 --> 00:18:29,713
SO YOU WON 30 EXTRA FRAMES
SO YOU HAVE

398
00:18:29,713 --> 00:18:31,581
A TOTAL OF 100 FRAMES TODAY.

399
00:18:31,581 --> 00:18:33,583
NAIMA DOESN'T NEED
30 EXTRA SHOTS.

400
00:18:33,583 --> 00:18:34,951
SHE'S A GREAT DANCER.

401
00:18:34,951 --> 00:18:36,953
SHE'LL PROBABLY GET IT
ON THE FIRST SHOT.

402
00:18:36,953 --> 00:18:39,523
THEN, KEENYAH,
YOU WON 20 EXTRA FRAMES.

403
00:18:39,523 --> 00:18:41,992
AND, BRITTANY,
YOU HAVE TEN EXTRA FRAMES.

404
00:18:41,992 --> 00:18:44,494
AND, KAHLEN, YOU DON'T HAVE
ANY EXTRA FRAMES.

405
00:18:44,494 --> 00:18:46,663
THAT MEAN YOU GOTTA WORK
THE HARDEST.

406
00:18:46,663 --> 00:18:48,665
YOUR PHOTOGRAPHER TODAY
IS JOHAN WILKE.

407
00:18:48,665 --> 00:18:50,667
HE HAS SHOT
FOR A LOT OF INTERNATIONAL

408
00:18:50,667 --> 00:18:51,868
FASHION MAGAZINES.

409
00:18:51,868 --> 00:18:53,804
TODAY WE'RE GONNA HAVE
PEOPLE DANCING.

410
00:18:53,804 --> 00:18:57,040
I THINK IT'S IMPORTANT
JUST TO BE YOURSELF, UH, RELAX.

411
00:18:57,040 --> 00:19:01,478
BUT YOU'RE GONNA BE DANCING
WITH THREE HOT GUYS.

412
00:19:04,247 --> 00:19:06,216
SO THESE ARE YOUR GUYS TODAY.

413
00:19:06,216 --> 00:19:07,884
HELLO.

414
00:19:07,884 --> 00:19:10,787
LEE-ROY, BERTINI, AND MARK.

415
00:19:14,357 --> 00:19:16,493
SO LET'S GO
TO HAIR AND MAKEUP.

416
00:19:23,667 --> 00:19:24,801
NO.

417
00:19:24,801 --> 00:19:26,069
SO DO YOU WANT TO GO OUT?

418
00:19:26,069 --> 00:19:27,103
DON'T WE, GUYS?

419
00:19:27,103 --> 00:19:28,138
DON'T WE WANT TO GO OUT?

420
00:19:28,138 --> 00:19:29,873
MM-HMM, I WANT TO GO OUT.

421
00:19:29,873 --> 00:19:32,909
WE WANT TO KNOW
HOW PARTYING IS IN SOUTH AFRICA.

422
00:19:32,909 --> 00:19:33,977
OH, YEAH.

423
00:19:33,977 --> 00:19:37,147
IT'LL BE FUN TO GO OUT
WITH THE GUYS FOR DINNER.

424
00:19:37,147 --> 00:19:40,250
WE DON'T GET A LOT OF
INTERACTION WITH OTHER PEOPLE.

425
00:19:40,250 --> 00:19:41,351
BERTINI?

426
00:19:41,351 --> 00:19:42,385
BERTINI, IT'S EASY.

427
00:19:42,385 --> 00:19:43,386
IT'S KIND OF A COOL NAME.

428
00:19:43,386 --> 00:19:45,188
I LIKE THAT NAME.

429
00:19:45,188 --> 00:19:46,389
UH, IT'S KEENYAH?

430
00:19:46,389 --> 00:19:48,592
BERTINI IS
A VERY INTERESTING PERSON.

431
00:19:48,592 --> 00:19:50,827
BEFORE WE GO ONTO THE SHOOT,
LIKE HE'S VERY, VERY FLIRTY.

432
00:19:50,827 --> 00:19:52,796
DO YOU WANT TO GIVE ME
YOUR NUMBER?

433
00:19:52,796 --> 00:19:53,830
I DON'T HAVE ONE.

434
00:19:53,830 --> 00:19:54,831
NO NUMBER?

435
00:19:54,831 --> 00:19:55,832
OKAY, I'LL GIVE YOU MINE.

436
00:19:55,832 --> 00:19:57,834
DO YOU WANT ME
TO TAKE YOUR PICTURE ON MY CELL?

437
00:19:57,834 --> 00:19:59,836
HE'S TRYING TO GET
MY PHONE NUMBER AND HE'S TRYING

438
00:19:59,836 --> 00:20:01,938
TO TAKE A PICTURE OF ME
ON HIS CAMERA PHONE,

439
00:20:01,938 --> 00:20:04,541
AND, UM, IT WAS VERY AWKWARD.

440
00:20:04,541 --> 00:20:06,209
WILL YOU GIVE ME
THAT MASSAGE?

441
00:20:06,209 --> 00:20:08,178
KEENYAH, HE WANTS
A MASSAGE FROM YOU.

442
00:20:08,178 --> 00:20:13,149
SORRY, GOTTA GO RUN
TO WARDROBE AFTER THIS.

443
00:20:13,250 --> 00:20:15,886
YOU NEED TO GO
MICKEY D's-STYLE.

444
00:20:15,886 --> 00:20:18,121
YOU KNOW, I NEED TO
REALLY WATCH WHAT I EAT

445
00:20:18,121 --> 00:20:20,390
SO THAT I CAN GET MY BODY BACK
TO HOW IT WAS

446
00:20:20,390 --> 00:20:22,492
WHEN I FIRST ENTERED
THE COMPETITION.

447
00:20:22,492 --> 00:20:27,030
I FEEL LIKE I AM PRETTY MUCH
STICKING TO MY DIET.

448
00:20:27,030 --> 00:20:29,065
IF THERE ARE ONLY FRENCH FRIES
TO EAT,

449
00:20:29,065 --> 00:20:31,034
I JUST EAT A SMALL AMOUNT
OF FRENCH FRIES.

450
00:20:31,968 --> 00:20:35,672
I THINK THAT SHE HASN'T BEEN
PAYING ATTENTION TO A LOT

451
00:20:35,672 --> 00:20:38,975
OF THE THINGS SHE'S PUTTING
IN HER MOUTH.

452
00:20:42,112 --> 00:20:43,647
ARE YOU READY THERE, NAIMA?

453
00:20:43,647 --> 00:20:44,648
YOU WANT TO DANCE,
YOU'RE GONNA HAVE SOME FUN.

454
00:20:44,648 --> 00:20:46,082
YOU LOOK GREAT, ALL RIGHT?

455
00:20:46,082 --> 00:20:47,951
SO, YOU KNOW,
HAVE FUN WITH THIS.

456
00:20:47,951 --> 00:20:49,419
COULD WE HAVE SOME MUSIC?

457
00:20:49,419 --> 00:20:53,123
(playing drums)
(singing in African language)

458
00:20:53,123 --> 00:20:56,626
CLOSE IN. HERE WE GO.

459
00:20:56,626 --> 00:20:59,863
